                                    <p><strong>ACFM Solution:</strong> Rope access ACFM inspection of all 250 nodes completed in 45 days (5-6 nodes/day) with platform in full production. ACFM through existing epoxy coating (3-5mm thick) detected 47 fatigue cracks (2-8mm depth). Detailed ACFM sizing enabled fracture mechanics ECA per BS 7910—33 cracks acceptable for continued service with annual ACFM monitoring; 14 cracks required weld repair (localized coating removal only at repair zones).</p>
                                    <p><strong>Outcome:</strong> Life extension approved based on ACFM data. Total inspection cost: $2.1M versus $20M+ for traditional MPI program. Zero production loss. Ongoing annual ACFM crack growth monitoring validates fracture mechanics predictions, supporting risk-based inspection optimization. Estimated 20-year extended production value: $1.5 billion.</p>
                                </div>
