                            <div class="tab-text">
                                <h3>Pipeline & Riser Weld Inspection</h3>
                                <p>Onshore and offshore pipeline girth welds, riser connections, and stress concentration zones (bends, tees, reducers) experience fatigue cracking from pressure cycling, vibration, and thermal expansion. ACFM detects cracks through pipeline coatings (FBE, 3-layer PE, tape, concrete weight coating) without excavation or coating removal—enabling targeted repair of only crack-affected zones versus blind weld replacement based on age/risk scoring.</p>
                                <ul class="checkmark-list">
                                    <li><i class="fas fa-check"></i> Onshore transmission pipeline girth welds through coating</li>
                                    <li><i class="fas fa-check"></i> Offshore export pipeline shore approach and subsea welds</li>
                                    <li><i class="fas fa-check"></i> Platform riser top connection fatigue (splash zone, deck penetration)</li>
                                    <li><i class="fas fa-check"></i> Flexible riser end fitting fatigue (stress concentration)</li>
                                    <li><i class="fas fa-check"></i> Pipeline repair sleeve/clamp weld integrity verification</li>
                                    <li><i class="fas fa-check"></i> Hot tap branch connection HAZ and weld toe cracks</li>
