                                    <li><i class="fas fa-check"></i> Subsea pipeline field joint coating damage assessment</li>
                                    <li><i class="fas fa-check"></i> LNG/LPG cryogenic pipeline weld thermal fatigue</li>
                                </ul>
                                <div class="app-highlight"> <i class="fas fa-hard-hat"></i>
                                    <div> <strong>Excavation Cost Avoidance:</strong>
                                        <p>Buried pipeline inspection traditionally requires excavation (backhoe, hydro-vac, hand digging depending on depth/sensitivity), coating removal, NDT, repair/accept decision, backfill, and coating restoration. Cost: $50K-200K per excavation depending on depth, soil conditions, environmental permits, and traffic control (road crossings). ACFM deployed in excavation enables immediate crack assessment through coating—accept crack if subcritical (backfill immediately, $50K saved), or proceed with repair if critical. On 100-location integrity dig program, ACFM through-coating screening identifies 20-30% requiring coating removal for repair versus 100% coating removal for blind MPI—saving $3M-10M in coating restoration costs. ACFM also enables in-ditch crack growth monitoring during hydrotest or operational pressure testing—measure crack before/after pressurization confirming stability or identifying unstable growth requiring action.</p>
