                                </ul>
                                <div class="app-highlight"> <i class="fas fa-industry"></i>
                                    <div> <strong>Fireproofing Preservation:</strong>
                                        <p>Refinery and petrochemical structural steel requires fireproofing (intumescent paint, cementitious spray, mineral wool boards) per API RP 2218 providing 1-4 hour fire resistance for safe personnel egress and emergency response. Fireproofing removal for weld inspection requires: certified contractor mobilization, containment (negative pressure enclosure), material testing (asbestos in older fireproofing), disposal as hazardous waste, NDT, weld repair if needed, fireproofing reapplication (spray or board), cure time (7-30 days), and final inspection/certification. Cost: $100K-500K per structural node. ACFM through fireproofing (up to 6mm spray or paint) eliminates this entire scope—inspect in-situ with facility in operation, zero fireproofing disturbance, immediate results. Refinery turnaround inspection example: 500 structural connections ACFM-screened in 2 weeks versus 6 months for fireproofing removal/replacement; only 20-30 crack-confirmed connections require localized fireproofing removal for weld repair access—saving $30M-50M in fireproofing work scope and enabling shorter, more efficient turnarounds.</p>
